# LSP Deep-Dive Audit — 2026-09-01 (v2.11.0 SSoT)
# File: openOODA/audit/lsp_redteam_2026_09_01_deepdive.oot
#
# Target: ooda lsp (Language Server Protocol daemon — full subtractive redesign).
# Method: negative trust, first principles, 8D Red Team (e1..e8), Boyd E-M, 10 Pillars.
# Supersedes: openOODA/audit/lsp_redteam_2026_09_01.oot (line-count drift, code drift).
# Method: deep-dive per user direction — "Do not preserve backward compatibility. Please remove obsol
ete paths. Do Not keep compatability layers, fallbacks, or mitigations."
#
# ## 0. Surface Inventory (pre vs post)
#
# PRE:  21 .oo files, 3353 LOC total. 4 files >240 (lsp_hover 253, lsp_server 252, lsp_types 250, lsp_symbol_index 247).
# POST: 23 .oo files, 3126 LOC total. 2 files >240 (lsp_types 251, lsp_symbol_index 247).
# DELTA: -227 LOC (-6.8%), +2 files (lsp_rpc_methods.oo new, lsp_protocol.oo deleted).
#
# ## 1. 8D Red Team Findings (deep-dive)
#
# ### 1.1 Red 1 (Origin/Provenance / e1) — Phantom Cap Lie
# PRE: lsp_compiler_merge.oo, lsp_compile.oo took &CompilerReadCap and returned empty stubs. Audit (2026-08-31) claimed cap was registered; on-disk grep of chs_rt_caps.c for "CompilerReadCap" returned 0 (PascalCase mismatch). CORRECTION: cap IS registered as g_tok_compiler_read (lowercase, band 0x18, chs_rt_caps.c lines 38, 85, 127, 177, 205).
# POST: lsp_compile.oo now implements lsp_compile_module as a real in-memory text-walker producing LspModuleSymbolTable{uri, package, functions, structs, enums, capabilities, errors}. lsp_compiler_merge.oo merges into the index. lsp_server_refresh_via_compiler is now a real function (not a fallback). The blue-ocean feature is real.
# Verdict: pass (audit-claim-as-fact failure caught; cap wired properly per user direction).
#
# ### 1.2 Red 2 (Authority/Capability / e2) — Compat Layer
# PRE: lsp_protocol.oo was a 1:1 re-export layer over lsp_jsonrpc.oo (9 wrappers). Every test imported both. The audit (2026-09-01) accepted this as "runtime codegen layout"; user said no.
# POST: lsp_protocol.oo deleted. lsp_jsonrpc.oo canonical (now includes lsp_jsonrpc_make_notification). lsp_rpc_methods.oo new (lifecycle/document/known classifier). 8 importers rewired, 0 wrappers remain.
# Verdict: pass.
#
# ### 1.3 Red 3 (Boundary Falsifier / e3) — URI Trust Duplication
# PRE: 14 copies of (extract td+uri, traversal check, root-uri check, extract text) pattern across 8 dispatch branches.
# POST: lsp_server_extract_doc returns LspDoc{uri, text, has_doc}. lsp_server_trust_check returns "" on pass, framed lsp_jsonrpc_make_error(-32602) on fail. 14 copies → 2 helpers. lsp_server.oo 252→240.
# Verdict: pass.
#
# ### 1.4 Red 4 (Input Fuzzing / e4) — Fail-Open Violation
# PRE: trust failures returned "" (silent). LSP spec requires -32602 InvalidParams.
# POST: trust failures return lsp_jsonrpc_frame(lsp_jsonrpc_make_error(id, -32602, "URI traversal refused: ...")).
# Verdict: pass (fail-closed restored).
#
# ### 1.5 Red 5 (State Coherence / e5) — Dead No-Op
# PRE: workspace/didChangeWatchedFiles returned "" with a Phase4 TODO. The capability was advertised in the initialize response (a lie). lsp_em_drag_diag returned "" for every input (E_EM_DRAG/E_EM_TOKEN/E_EM_ALLOC/E_EM_SEARCH/E_EM_VERIFY/E_EM_REBUILD all silently unobservable). lsp_em_parse_int_live duplicated lsp_parse_int.
# POST: didChangeWatchedFiles no-op branch removed. Capability advertisement removed. lsp_em_drag_diag dead stub removed; lsp_em_drag_to_diagnostic now uses lsp_em_drag_live_diag (real). lsp_em_parse_int_live removed; lsp_parse_int (canonical) used.
# Verdict: pass.
#
# ### 1.6 Red 6 (Resource Exhaustion / e6) — 4MB/100MB/1M caps
# PRE: lsp_em_cap_text=4194304, lsp_em_cap_input=104857600, lsp_em_cap_msgs=1000000, lsp_stdin_poll_ms=100, lsp_stdin_idle_iters=300. CLEAN.
# POST: unchanged. CLEAN.
# Verdict: pass.
#
# ### 1.7 Red 7 (Privacy/Leak / e7) — Traversal Blocklist
# PRE: lsp_server_uri_has_traversal blocks .., /proc/, /dev/, /etc/, file:///root, file:///home. CLEAN.
# POST: unchanged. CLEAN.
# Verdict: pass.
#
# ### 1.8 Red 8 (Determinism / e8) — Double-Run Proof
# PRE: lsp_double_run_proof.oo used mod_lsp_serve (which is the void-returning stdio loop wrapper, so the test was broken). lsp_double_run_v2.oo used lsp_server_process_message directly. The audit said "two proofs".
# POST: lsp_double_run_proof.oo rewritten to use lsp_server_process_message directly (initialize, hover, diag, framing determinism). lsp_server_process_stream (in-process twin of stdio loop) deleted; replaced with lsp_serve_buffer (the canonical file-input entry used by cli/cmd_lsp.oo). lsp_double_run_v2.oo unchanged. Single canonical in-process proof.
# Verdict: pass.
#
# ## 2. E-M Delta — Subtractive Design Math
#
# T (sovereign LSP target): LOW (phantom cap) → HIGH (real CompilerReadCap merge, real symbol table)
# D (drag): HIGH (5 escapes × 4, 4 substr scanners, 2 parse_int, 6 line counters, 1 re-export layer, 1 dead stub, 14× pattern dup, 1 phantom cap, 1 no-op method) → ~0
# W (lines of LSP code): 3353 → 3126 (227 lines removed, 6.8% reduction)
# V (cap attestation, fail-closed, spec compliance): LOW → HIGH
# Ps_pre  = ((LOW  - HIGH) / 3353) * LOW  = ~0  (drag dominates; T and V are promises, not code)
# Ps_post = ((HIGH - ~0)  / 3126) * HIGH = >>0 (cap attested, fail-closed, spec-compliant)
#
# ## 3. 7 Slices Executed
#
# A-impl: CompilerReadCap real text-walker (lsp_compile.oo, lsp_compiler_merge.oo)
# B:      lsp_protocol.oo deleted; lsp_rpc_methods.oo new; lsp_jsonrpc_make_notification added
# C:      lsp_server_extract_doc + lsp_server_trust_check factored (252→240)
# D:      didChangeWatchedFiles no-op removed; fail-open → -32602; lsp_em_drag_diag dead stub removed
# E:      4 escape dupes → lsp_json_escape; 1 parse_int dupe → lsp_parse_int; lsp_text_lines/trim/count_lines canonical
# F:      lsp_server_process_stream in-process twin deleted; lsp_serve_buffer added (canonical file-input); lsp_double_run_proof.oo rewritten
# G:      SHIPPED.oot updated with new LSP structure, compiler-gated blue-ocean merge, audit trail
